Day 30 of my 120-day Data Analytics challenge

The goal is simple but powerful:
Use data to understand what might influence the success or failure of a crowdfunding campaign.

Today I continued working on my SQL project analyzing Kickstarter campaigns, stepping further into the role of a data analyst.

Some of the things I worked on included:
• Exploring the dataset using SQL queries
• Filtering projects by category and performance
• Calculating funding percentages
• Using CASE statements to classify campaign funding levels

Key Insights from the Analysis

 i) Many failed campaigns were concentrated in categories such as Film & Video, Music, Food, Design, Publishing, and Crafts. 

ii) Projects with strong backer support and higher pledged amounts were more likely to succeed.

 iii) Several projects achieved less than 50% of their funding goal, especially in categories like Art, Games, Crafts, Music, Film & Video, Design, and Technology. 

iv) Using conditional logic helped categorize campaigns into Fully Funded, Nearly Funded, and Not Nearly Funded, making it easier to evaluate campaign performance. 


This project helped me practice how analysts turn raw data into insights that inform business decisions.

I’m excited to keep building my SQL skills and continue pushing forward toward Day 120. 🚀
